# Due letture della stessa parola devono restare visibili senza scegliere
# per ordine. I contatti e la correzione sono ordinari; nessun ponte seminato.
# Contratto fissato prima della cura, 25 settembre 2026.
[mock live]
!set PARROT0_SESSION=
!set PARROT0_PROFILE=kb/profiles/agi.p0
!set PARROT0_LANG=en
!reset

[test una lettura utile nasce dal contatto]
!timeout 0
> Einstein was born in Ulm, so his Geburtsort is Ulm.
> What is the Geburtsort of Napoleon?
<~ ajaccio

[test un uso incompatibile non autorizza due significati globali]
!timeout 0
> Steel is made of iron, so iron is its Geburtsort.
!query contact_episode(geburtsort, born_in, $E)
!query contact_episode(geburtsort, made_of, $E)
!query! contact_bridge(geburtsort, born_in)
!query! contact_bridge(geburtsort, made_of)
> What is the Geburtsort of paper?
<~ competing readings
<! wood
> What is the Geburtsort of Napoleon?
<~ competing readings
<! ajaccio

[test un controesempio distingue e riattiva la lettura restante]
!timeout 0
> Glass is made of sand, but sand is not its Geburtsort.
!query contact_counter(geburtsort, made_of, $E)
!query contact_bridge(geburtsort, born_in)
!query! contact_bridge(geburtsort, made_of)
> What is the Geburtsort of Napoleon?
<~ Reading
<~ ajaccio
!query made_of(glass, sand)
!query born_in(einstein, ulm)

[test il ritiro dell'ultimo ponte toglie di nuovo la lettura]
!timeout 0
!assert contact_bridge_withdrawn(geburtsort, born_in)
> What is the Geburtsort of Napoleon?
<! ajaccio
!query contact_episode(geburtsort, born_in, $E)
!query contact_episode(geburtsort, made_of, $E)

[test ordine opposto e parola diversa: non vince la prima ipotesi]
!timeout 0
> Steel is made of iron, so iron is its Herkunft.
> Einstein was born in Ulm, so his Herkunft is Ulm.
!query contact_episode(herkunft, made_of, $E)
!query contact_episode(herkunft, born_in, $E)
!query! contact_bridge(herkunft, made_of)
!query! contact_bridge(herkunft, born_in)
> What is the Herkunft of paper?
<~ competing readings
<! wood
> What is the Herkunft of Napoleon?
<~ competing readings
<! ajaccio
> Glass is made of sand, but sand is not its Herkunft.
> What is the Herkunft of Napoleon?
<~ Reading
<~ ajaccio

[test stessa revisione per i verbi e le viste del lettore condiviso]
!timeout 0
> Einstein was born in Ulm, so he hails from Ulm.
> Where does Napoleon hail from?
<~ Ajaccio
> Steel is made of iron, so it hails from iron.
!query contact_episode(hails, born_in, $E)
!query contact_episode(hails, made_of, $E)
!query! answer_frame(hails, born_in)
!query! answer_frame(hail, born_in)
!query! construction_frame("@S hails from @O", $K, born_in)
> Where does Napoleon hail from?
<~ competing readings
<! Ajaccio
# Ablazione tecnica dichiarata: il ritiro naturale e' provato sopra sui nomi.
!assert contact_bridge_withdrawn(hails, made_of)
!query answer_frame(hail, born_in)
> Where does Napoleon hail from?
<~ Reading
<~ Ajaccio
